            <ArticleTitle>Peripheral ulcerative keratitis in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>486-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaapos.2011.06.009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Peripheral ulcerative keratitis is a destructive process involving perilimbal corneal inflammation and an overlying epithelial defect. It can be a manifestation of systemic autoimmune diseases or can be secondary to an infectious process. We present a case of a 7-year-old girl with peripheral ulcerative keratitis of unknown etiology. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first such case reported in a child.</AbstractText>
